==English==

===Etymology===
From radio communications phrase dating from the 1950s. The first five referred to a rating of signal clarity, the other to reception strength. See {{w|Signal strength and readability report}}.

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|five by five}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-|head=[[five]]-[[by]]-[[five]]}}

# [[loud and clear]]
# [[fine]]; [[OK]]

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|basketball}} A performance in which a player accumulates a total of five in five statistical categories — [[point]]s, [[rebound]]s, [[assist]]s, [[steal]]s{{,}} and [[block]]s — in a single game.

